    	The idea is pretty simple.  The sculptor's kit is a tool with a 
limited number of uses, kind of like a tinning kit.  When you use it you 
must have a rock in your inventory.  Then it prompts you to select a 
monster in your line of sight.  If that monster stays still for 20 turns 
(you can't finish sculpting if your model moves), the rock is used up and 
becomes a figurine of the target monster.  Otherwise the rock is discarded.  
Either way, a charge is used up on the sculpting kit.

    	What do you think?  I thought there should be a way to get figurines 
besides finding them or wishing for them, both of which apply to all items.  
You should be able to manufacture them like tins.  Also, it isn't that easy 
to do, because you'd need to get the monster to stay still for 20 turns ... 
whether it's trapping it in a bear trap, putting it to sleep, paralyzing 
it, stoning it, etc.

